; ============================================================================
; monitor.sasm -- STAGE 5/6: the real supervisor-mode monitor.
; -
; Reached only via EXCP from the main program in crc-report.sasm, which runs
; in protected mode throughout (see the comment above :main there). Two user
; trap vectors are wired into the vector table by crc-report.sasm's own
; .ORG/.DW block at word addresses 0x100/0x101 (vector 0x80) and 0x102/0x103
; (vector 0x81) -- see the comment there for why a single ".DW @label" is a
; complete vector-table entry.
; -
; Calling convention (this program's own design; the manual leaves calling
; conventions entirely out of scope -- see Chapter 3/6):
; -
;   EXCP #0x80 ("write_word"): r1 = word offset (0-based) within the
;     report_file segment (0x00E00000, wired up via the Makefile's --segment
;     flag); r2 = the 16-bit value to write there. This program always
;     passes a single ASCII digit byte, zero-extended to a full word,
;     matching itoa5's own word-per-digit buffer layout. This handler
;     performs the actual privileged cross-segment write -- writing ah
;     directly is exactly the operation protected mode forbids the caller,
;     which is the entire reason this trap exists. Clobbers the shared
;     (unbanked) ah/al registers; the caller never relies on `a` surviving a
;     call. Touches no other registers.
; -
;   EXCP #0x81 ("halt"): no arguments. Ends the simulation via the
;     simulator's COP 0x14FF hook (see NOTES.md "simulation-termination
;     discovery"). Issued from here, in supervisor mode, purely so the main
;     program never has to leave protected mode itself just to halt.
; ============================================================================

:monitor_entry
    LOAD ah, #0x00E0
    LOAD al, r1
    STOR (#0, a), r2
    RETE

:monitor_halt
    COPI #0x14FF                  ; simulator-recognized "abort simulation" call
    RETE                           ; unreachable -- COPI #0x14FF ends the run
